# Citation File Format 1.2.0, https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# At each release, version follows muse_tmr.__version__ and date-released the date of that
# version in CHANGELOG.md; tests/test_packaging.py checks both, and CI runs cffconvert --validate.
# DOI: pending. It comes with the first release archived on Zenodo, which the maintainer has
# not set up yet (#232); add it here as doi: once it exists.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use REMind in research, please cite the version you used, and amused-py
  as well when you use its BLE layer (muse_tmr.ble). REMind is n = 1 research
  software, not a medical device.
type: software
title: "REMind: REM-gated targeted memory reactivation for the Muse S Athena EEG headset"
abstract: >-
  Overnight recording, offline replay, real-time REM detection and safety-gated
  audio cues for the Muse S Athena EEG headset, with the single-subject protocol
  around them: pre-sleep puzzles with seeded cued and uncued groups, REM-gated
  cueing, morning dream reports, blind retests and a descriptive cued-vs-uncued
  analysis. n = 1 research software, not a medical device; it makes no clinical,
  diagnostic, therapeutic or lucid-dreaming claims.
authors:
  - family-names: Mikityuk
    given-names: Yuriy
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yuriy-mikityuk/remind-eeg"
url: "https://github.com/yuriy-mikityuk/remind-eeg"
keywords:
  - muse
  - eeg
  - sleep
  - targeted-memory-reactivation
  - lucid-dreaming
  - research-software
references:
